{
 "format": "bgsim.subsystem",
 "name": "F16Airframe",
 "description": "One F-16 (Stevens & Lewis) in calm air, without landing gear: the multibond rigid body on a free joint (principal axes), the air data, the NASA aerodynamic tables, the force build-up and the engine. Inputs el, ail, rdr (deg) and thtl (0..1); outputs the air data, nz and the pose, and the energy-audit taps gP, VP, P_ext. The defaults are the open-loop trim (502 ft/s, sea level) at xcg 0.35; an instance sets the CG (Forces/xcg) and its start state (Free/*, Body/inertia/P, Engine/P). Generated by design/build_model.py.",
